      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T06:40:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heh, well, with the original command stream implementation it was trivial. :-)  That simplicity of transporting, saving, and replaying is lost with the move to ioctl().\n\nThat said it\u0027s certainly still possible.  Userspace can serialize and deserialize the ioctls into a message stream.  I\u0027ve been wanting to provide a standalone program for that, reusing the original command stream format.  It could also serve as a canonical example pseudo controller implementation.\n\nIn addition to trivially sending over the network or any kind of pipe, a streaming format like the original UAPI also allows for really simple I2C device driver regression tests when precise timing isn\u0027t a concern.  Simply replay a saved file of transactions and consider any deviation a failure.",
