      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T06:40:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s an existing thing, I2C adapters are expected to have a timeout and not wait forever for a response.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/upstream/include/linux/i2c.h;drc\u003d5eb1e6e459cfa025f79c43014f66ff62a55542f1;l\u003d730\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/upstream/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c;drc\u003d564d73c4d9201526bd976b9379d2aaf1a7133e84;l\u003d1499-1501\n\ni2c-pseudo respects the timeout, and also lets userspace configure it (via `timeout_ms` field of `struct i2cp_ioctl_start_arg`).  I think most pseudo controllers will or should set a custom timeout, curated for the expected latency of whatever they\u0027re doing.\n\nThink this should be explained here in the doc?  Or okay to assume this knowledge?",
      "parentUuid": "9b47661f_85ab031c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 77
