      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T18:01:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "does it make sense to provide short summary of the below while going into details. \n\n\nSummary:\n\n\"This section provides detailed instructions on how to use the userspace I2C adapter. It covers creating and destroying adapters, handling I2C transactions, using polling, and shutting down the adapter.\"\n\nExplanation\n\n1) Creating and Destroying adapter\n\nTo create a new I2C adapter, open the /dev/i2c-pseudo device file and call the I2CP_IOCTL_START ioctl. The adapter will continue to exist until its file descriptor is closed. Multiple pseudo adapters can be used simultaneously.\n\n2) Handling I2C Transactions\n\n3) Using Polling\n\nPolling is supported for both blocking and non-blocking operation. The ``POLLIN`` event indicates that an I2C transaction is available for ``I2CP_IOCTL_XFER_REQ``. The POLLOUT event indicates that ``I2CP_IOCTL_XFER_REPLY`` may be valid. The ``POLLHUP`` event indicates that ``I2CP_IOCTL_SHUTDOWN`` has been called.\n\n4) Shutting Down the Adapter",
