      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T15:21:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@amstan@chromium.org @swboyd@chromium.org Let me know what you think of the shared `data_buf` concept.\n\nNot having `data_buf` would of course simplify this API struct, as well as the kernel side implementation of I2CP_IOCTL_XFER_REQ.  However then userspace would have to preallocate fixed-sized buffers for each i2c_msg, so less efficient use of memory.  It might also be clunkier for userspace, since then i2c_msg.len would be used as both input (size of available buffer) and output (actual size used), thus needing to be filled in again for each I2CP_IOCTL_XFER_REQ call.",
      "revId": "22dbe7ee3a9b98fb20292b59dade5e220db083e3",
